export anchor AcademicPaperStyle:
    number: 39
    screen: ProjectDetail
    name: Academic paper
    idea: The project page is typeset like a journal article, with a centred title block, an abstract, numbered sections, ruled tables, a captioned figure and footnotes.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #fdfdfb, the page
        ink: #111111, text, rules, the primary button and the figure bar
        grey: #555555, affiliation, dates, assignees and meta text
        rule: #b8b8b8, the hairline rule between the two columns
        citationRed: #8a1c1c, links, footnote marks and file names
        shade: #f0efea, the fill of a focused list row
    type:
        One Computer Modern-like serif, "Latin Modern Roman", "CMU Serif",
        "Century Schoolbook", "TeX Gyre Schola", Georgia, "Times New
        Roman", serif. File names use "Latin Modern Mono", "Courier New",
        monospace. Sizes are 30px regular centred for the title, 18px bold
        numbered section heads, 16px body at 1.45 line height and justified
        with hyphens, 15px small caps for status words, 13px captions and
        footnotes, and 11px superscript marks.
    layout:
        A thin running head across the top holds Brightwork in small caps,
        italic nav links, a search field drawn as an underline and the
        user name, over a 0.5px rule. The article is 980px wide and centred.
        It opens with a journal line, the title, the three members as
        authors with the owner starred, the team as affiliation, a date and
        status line, and two buttons. A narrow abstract holds the brief and
        a keywords line. The body then runs in two text columns from 900px
        with a hairline column rule. Section 1 Summary has a bar figure and
        a facts table, 2 Milestones a ruled table, 3 Open tasks a numbered
        list, 4 Files a bracketed reference list, and 5 Discussion a quote
        and a reply field. Footnotes sit under a short rule at the end.
        Below 900px the body is one column.
    spacing: Tight book leading. 8px between paragraphs with a 1.5em first-line indent, 20px above section heads and a 36px column gap.
    density: Dense like print. The whole screen fits in about one and a half wide screens.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders: Booktabs tables with 1.2px top and bottom rules, a 0.6px rule under the header row, and no vertical lines. Buttons and fields have a 0.8px ink border.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        No pictograms. Typographic marks sit beside every status word, a
        tick for done and on track, a half circle for in progress, an open
        circle for planned and a slashed circle for blocked. The progress
        figure is a filled bar beside an outlined bar with a numbered axis.
    focus: A 1px dashed ink outline offset 3px. A focused list row also takes the shade fill.
    tone: Formal third person with captions, such as Four tasks remain open, and Table 2. Milestones and their state.
